      "title": "Google excludes Spirit Airlines worker files from $10 million AI data deal",
      "content_html": "Google agreed to exclude Spirit Airlines employee medical, disciplinary, drug-testing and safety records from its planned $10 million purchase of the bankrupt carrier’s digital archives after unions objected to the use of workers’ personal information to train artificial-intelligence models. The revised terms led unions representing former employees to withdraw their objections, but the sale still requires approval from a bankruptcy judge at a Nov. 17 hearing in New York.\n\nSpirit will hire Tonic AI to remove identifying details, and an independent reviewer will check the process. Google also agreed to keep the data confidential and not attempt to identify individuals. The sale still includes corporate records such as emails and Microsoft Teams messages, which Google wants to use to improve its products and AI models.",
