      "title": "New Apple TV box supports four HomePods and smart home control",
      "content_html": "Apple has been selling the fourth-generation Apple TV 4K since November 13. It also serves as a smart home hub. In Germany, the streaming box costs 349 euros; for the first time, it can be connected to up to four HomePod speakers to create a home theater system.\n\nHomeKit and Matter devices such as lights, cameras, locks, and thermostats that are set up through the Home app can be controlled via Apple TV. On compatible cameras, the TV can display a live feed. Doorbells can show notifications, allowing users to speak with visitors and open the door. The built-in far-field microphones enable voice commands without a remote control—in testing, Siri turned off Philips Hue lights, for example.\n\nThe new Siri AI is of limited use to many users in Germany: it requires a paired Apple device with Siri AI enabled. Siri AI is not yet available on iPhones and iPads in the EU. German is also not supported. Apple has not given a specific date for an update bringing Siri AI to older Apple TV models.",
